          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em spectral super-scheme
            is supposed to be the refinement of the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-scheme"} super-scheme
            as one passes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"} spectral geometry
            in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+rings"} E-infinity rings
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+geometry"}> E-infinity geometry
            ).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The following is an argument for a good definition of spectral supergeometry. This was originally motivated from the observation in
            %a{:href => "#Kapranov13"} Kapranov 13
            and uses results due to
            %a{:href => "#Rezk09"} Rezk 09
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SagaveSchlichtkrull11"} Sagave-Schlichtkrull 2011
          %p Observe that
          %ol
            %li#EInfinityGeometryAlreadyZGraded
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+geometry"}
